{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110027","id":2778790676,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6loPsU","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110027","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110027.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110027.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110027","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110027/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110027/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110027/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e40436d5271b7286b20ffd5519d3039d7016cc2a","number":110027,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":" Switch LOD generation to use iterative simplification","user":{"login":"zeux","id":1106629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDY2Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1106629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Instead of simplifying every LOD from the original down to an\r\nincreasing number of triangles, we simplify each LOD from the previous\r\nLOD and stop when the simplification can't proceed further.\r\n\r\nThis has a few benefits:\r\n\r\n- It's significantly faster; using sparse flag helps ensure that\r\n  subsequent simplifications after the first one are increasingly\r\n  cheaper.\r\n\r\n- It results in higher quality attributes on generated LODs; attribute\r\n  quadrics reduce the quality of attribute preservation the more they\r\n  are accumulated, so recomputing them from intermediate geometry helps.\r\n\r\n- It results in monotonic appearance: if a feature is reduced in a\r\n  higher LOD, it will stay reduced or get reduced more significantly in\r\n  lower LODs. This is not a significant problem right now, but can be\r\n  helpful to ensure if the number of LODs increases or some newer\r\n  features get enabled.\r\n\r\nAfter this change, the set of generated LODs will be a little different, as the number\r\nof triangles the simplifier is given is naturally distinct - however, the behavior\r\nin general should be more or less consistent. Now that generating more LODs is\r\nquite cheap, we can explore making LODs a little more frequent (e.g. doing 1.6x steps\r\ninstead of 2x steps) in the future.\r\n\r\nJust like previously, on some models we end up reducing the LOD 2x and generating\r\na significantly steeper error, whereas a 1.6x reduction could result in a more reasonable\r\nerror. This is something we can explore fixing in the future (for example, if a given simplification\r\nproduced an error that's more than 3x the previous error, we can attempt to rerun it with a\r\nsmaller target, which is now easy and fairly cheap). To reduce the complexity of this change,\r\nit doesn't do that.\r\n\r\nTesting this on a 100-model variant from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/93587,\r\nI get 25 seconds to import before this change, and 17 seconds after. This, however, doesn't\r\ntell the full story: before this change, the simplification time during the import is 11 seconds,\r\nand after this change it's just 3!\r\n\r\n0.5 out of 3 seconds after this change is spent outside of `meshopt_simplify` in various hashmap\r\ncode. This can be improved in the future / separately; that all will be unnecessary if we switch\r\nto permissive simplification, but that will probably be in 4.7 timeframe.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310502,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA1MDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:import","name":"topic:import","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url"